- Story & Context: Written for Mireille Dufour, a night-shift telegraph operator in Charleroi who secretly copied railway clearance logs to help political dissidents slip across the border, the track centers on a hypnotic single-chord accordion drone that sustains uninterrupted for nine minutes. During the session, Dufour burst into the freezing rehearsal room smelling of lamp paraffin to announce the secret police had raided her transit locker and confiscated the correspondence she had hidden alongside the original time capsule canister. Without stopping his rhythmic thumb-picking, Vaneau watched Dufour pack her rucksack and delivered her devastating confession straight into the ribbon mic: "You stamped my departure before my boots even touched the stone." The master reel caught the exact pitch wobble of the dying tape deck's capstan, immortalizing the panic of her escape in a slow-motion acoustic hum.
