Track 3: Capstan Flutter at the Junction
- Story & Context: According to scene lore, this closing track was cut in the defunct signal tower at Schaerbeek during the final hours before municipal wrecking balls leveled the depot. Kroll weighted the accordion’s lower reeds with brass railway keys and let the instrument breathe on its own while the band piped the audio through the water-rotted capsule tape, allowing the physical mold on the ribbon to chew holes into the high frequencies. As the tape leader tore apart at the final chorus, an anonymous voice from an open dispatch telephone line broke through the monitors to deliver the closing myth: "Nothing departs on time when the clock is carved from coal." The musicians left the tape deck running, locked the tower door, and walked into the morning fog, leaving the master to spin itself to dust.
